<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Battle of the Marne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marne">Marne</a> was fought in September 1914, when French and British forces halted the German advance towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. It ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>'s hopes of a quick victory in the west and led to the years of trench warfare on the Western Front.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-the-marne.jpg" alt="First Battle of the Marne" width="320" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: German Army · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:German_soldiers_Battle_of_Marne_WWI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
